WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.620
Effective detection engineering combines technical knowledge, operational awareness,

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.000
collaboration, and humility.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Teams should remain curious, test assumptions, seek feedback, document decisions,

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.500
and improve practices over time.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.000
A healthy culture treats detections as living products.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.000
They have users, dependencies, maintenance needs, and quality expectations.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.250
This mindset helps teams build detections that analysts can understand and trust.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.730
Sustainable capability requires shared ownership.

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:29.190
Security engineers, SIEM administrators, analysts, hunters, responders,

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.500
infrastructure teams, application owners,

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.970
and managers all contribute different context that improves detection work.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.500
The objective is not perfection.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:41.075
The objective is creating a durable capability that helps defenders identify, investigate,

00:00:41.075 --> 00:00:45.990
and respond to suspicious activity efficiently while adapting as the organization changes.
